&lt;h2&gt;


  Why "Figma Dev Mode" Didn't Solve the Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When Figma launched Dev Mode, developers hoped for a revolution. What we got was an inspector that tells us:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* Figma Dev Mode Output */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;342px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;48px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;120px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;top&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;240px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;#1961ED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;border-radius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Absolute coordinates? Hardcoded pixel widths? Zero responsive flexbox wrapping? No gesture interruptions?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dev Mode didn't kill design handoff—it just made redlining dead pixels more expensive.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  How ExodeUI Solves the Equation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ExodeUI takes a radically different stance: &lt;strong&gt;Design what you ship. Ship what you design.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
