&lt;h1&gt;


  Canvas vs DOM in 2026: Why Complex Dashboards Are Ditching Divs
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every frontend engineer knows the DOM threshold: 100 components run at 60fps; 2,000 components cause catastrophic layout reflows and memory thrashing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why DOM Scales Poorly with Dense Data
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In standard DOM rendering, modifying a single style triggers a full reflow pipeline:&lt;br&gt;
Style Recalculation ➔ Layout Geometry ➔ Paint ➔ Composite.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Virtual Scenegraph
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Canvas eliminates DOM node allocation. Instead, a lightweight spatial index (R-Tree / Quadtree) queries visible nodes in $O(\log N)$ time and renders them in a single draw batch.&lt;/p&gt;

